This feature/refactor branch adds support for `MULTIPOLYGON` but also greatly streamlines the code needed to translate both sp and sf objects to Leaflet polygon data. See the giant comment in normalize.R, but the gist is that for any sp/sf object you only need to implement the most "natural" method among `to_ring`, `to_polygon`, `to_multipolygon`, or `to_multipolygon_list`, and rely on the default implementation of these methods to properly "box" the data the correct number of times (this was very tricky to get right previously).

`MULTIPOINT` is still not supported, but that's because I don't currently know how to implement the JS side without breaking clustering and crosstalk. At best we figure out a way to do this well, maybe by translating `MULTIPOINT` to `POINT` somewhere along the line; at worst we may need to add a new R function for adding this kind of data, that doesn't provide clustering or possibly even crosstalk.

