This is a pull request to add support for adding and removing leaflet controls with arbitrary html content. [See the demo here.](https://plourde.shinyapps.io/addControl-demo/addControl-demo.Rmd)

This branch adds the file **R/controls.R** with the following definition of `addControl`:

``` r
addControl = function(map, 
    position=c('topleft', 'topright', 'bottomleft', 'bottomright'), 
    html, 
    controlId=NULL,
    classes=c('info', 'legend'),
    data=getMapData(map)) {

    position <- 
        if (missing(position)) position[1]
        else position

    classes <- paste(classes, collapse=' ')
    html <- as.character(html);

    appendMapData(map, data, 'addControl', position, html, controlId, classes)
}
```

with correspoding javascript method in **inst/htmlwidgets/leaflet.js**

``` javascript
methods.addControl = function(position, html, controlId, classes) {
  var onAdd = function(map) {
    var div = L.DomUtil.create('div', classes);
    div.innerHTML = html;
    if (typeof controlId !== 'undefined' && controlId !== null) {
      div.setAttribute('id', controlId)
    }
    this._div = div;
    return this._div;
  };
  var Control = L.Control.extend({options: {position: position}, onAdd: onAdd})
  this.controls.add(new Control, controlId);
};
```

Additionally, I've added a new "store" for controls in **inst/htmlwidgets/leaflet.js**, `ControlStore`, that allows for their management. This store behaves similarly to the already existing `LayerStore`.

``` javascript
  function ControlStore(map) {
    this._controlsNoId = [];
    this._controlsById = {};
    this._map = map
  }

  ControlStore.prototype.add = function(control, id) {
    if (typeof(id) !== 'undefined' && id !== null) {
      if (this._controlsById[id]) {
        this._map.removeControl(this._controlsById[id]);
      }
      this._controlsById[id] = control;
    } else {
      this._controlsNoId.push(control)
    }
    this._map.addControl(control);
  };

  ControlStore.prototype.remove = function(id) {
    if (this._controlsById[id]) {
      this._map.removeControl(this._controlsById[id]);
      delete this._controlsById[id];
    }
  };

  ControlStore.prototype.clear = function() {
    for (var i = 0; i < this._controlsNoId.length; i++) {
        this._map.removeControl(this._controlsNoId[i]);
    };
    this._controlsNoId = [];

    for (var key in this._controlsById) {
        this._map.removeControl(this._controlsById[key])
    }
    this._controlsById = {}
  }
```

In order to fully support adding and removing controls via `leaflet:::leafletController`, I've modified the HTML widget `initialize` function so that it saves the `map` variable generated by leaflet during the initialization process in an attribute of the binding named `_map`. It's necessary to have access to this variable to call leaflet functions, such as `removeControl`, on the map outside of the `initialize` and `renderValue` functions. 

To get this variable in the leaflet custom message handler used by `leafletController`, I changed the line `var map = document.getElementById(mapId);` to `var map = Shiny.shinyapp.$bindings[mapId].binding._map`. I'm not sure if this is the easiest way to do this. These changes to the initialize function and the custom message handler also enable usage of the existing `remove*` methods defined in **inst/htmlwidgets/leaflet.js**, which, as far as I can tell, are not fully yet supported.
